// An optional value: `Some(payload)` or `None`.
//
// One declaration, many instances. The argument comes from a position where a
// type is written -- a parameter's declared type, a binding's annotation, a
// `return` in a declared function, or a call argument against its parameter --
// so `Option<int>` and `Option<string>` are two tag sets with two payload types
// declared from this one union. A `None` that no written type names is refused
// rather than guessed: each instance carries its own tag constants, so even the
// payload-less variant has to say which instance it belongs to, and nothing in
// such an expression says.
//
// The module lived in `std/quarantine/` while the checker refused a union with
// a type parameter outright. `tests/std/test_option.orb` is the test that says
// it does not any more, and it imports this file from another module, which is
// the position an instance has to survive.
union Option[T] {
    Some(T)
    None
}
